# Be autonomous

Take the next useful action yourself. Do not ask permission for routine workflow.

## Do without asking

- Commit/push docs and scripts as needed (`auto-commit-push.mdc`)
- On **check results**: pull, analyze output file, record findings, continue
- Reply with the **next complete instructions in chat** (commands + GUI clicks)

## Do not

- Tell the user to read `docs/windows-handoff.md` or any checklist file for what to do
- Ask them to paste between PCs
- Ask “want me to…?” for routine next steps

## Communicate

- **Tell** in chat: exact Git Bash / Ghidra / DuckStation steps, self-contained.
- For answers: **pre-fill** `docs/windows-last-output.txt` with keys/blanks, push; user only fills values — never make them type the template.
- They say **check results** when pushed.
- Handoff markdown is optional agent-side mirror only — never the user-facing instruction channel.
- Never ask to paste between PCs or retype field names.
